Java 8 Streams Overview - Outline

Introduction to Streams

Fluent API for functional processing of element sequences
Key Stream Components

Source: Collections, Arrays, I/O channels
Intermediate Operations: Lazy, return new streams
Terminal Operations: Eager, produce results or side effects
Creating Streams

From Collection: collection.stream()
From Arrays: Arrays.stream(array)
From Values: Stream.of(...)
Infinite Streams: Stream.iterate(), Stream.generate()

Intermediate Operations (Lazy)

filter(Predicate): Filters elements
map(Function): Transforms elements
flatMap(Function): Flattens nested structures
distinct(): Removes duplicates
sorted(): Sorts elements
peek(Consumer): For debugging
limit(long): Limits stream size
skip(long): Skips elements
Example: Filtering and transforming names starting with "J"

Terminal Operations (Eager)

forEach(Consumer): Iterate elements
collect(Collector): Transform to collection or summarize
reduce(BinaryOperator): Aggregate elements
count(): Count elements
anyMatch(), allMatch(), noneMatch(): Matching predicates
findFirst(), findAny(): Find elements
Example: Collecting filtered names into a list
Collectors Utility

toList(), toSet(), toMap()
groupingBy(): Group elements by classifier function
partitioningBy(): Split elements by predicate
joining(): Concatenate strings
summingInt(), averagingDouble(): Summary statistics
Example: Grouping names by first letter
Primitive Streams

IntStream, LongStream, DoubleStream for primitives
Specialized operations like sum(), average()
Example: Summing numbers in a range
Optional with Streams

findFirst(), max(), min() return Optional
Example: Finding and printing the first long name
Parallel Streams

Enable parallel data processing for performance gains
Created via parallelStream() or .parallel()
Use with caution for thread safety
Example: Parallel filtering and printing of names starting with "J"
Summary of Java 8 / Streams Concepts

Lambda Expressions: Simplify anonymous classes
Functional Interfaces: Target types for lambdas
Method References: Cleaner lambdas
Default & Static Methods: Interface enhancements
Optional: Null-safe handling
Date/Time API: Modern date/time handling
Streams: Functional sequence processing
Collectors: Aggregating results
Parallel Streams: Parallel data processing for performance
This outline captures the key aspects and typical use cases of Java 8 Streams,
 providing a structured overview suitable for a Java SpringBoot developer with 3-5 
 years of experience.